RHACS Policies Repository

This repository contains SecurityPolicy manifests for Red Hat Advanced Cluster Security (RHACS) / StackRox and is managed via ArgoCD.

Repository Structure
rhacs_policies/
└── deploy/
    └── require-readonly-rootfs.yaml   # Example SecurityPolicy
argocd-app.yaml                        # ArgoCD Application manifest
argocd-rbac.yaml                        # ArgoCD ServiceAccount + RoleBinding
README.md                               # This documentation

1. Install RHACS Operator

Login to OpenShift:

oc login --token=<token> --server=<server>


Create the RHACS namespace:

oc create namespace stackrox


Install the RHACS Operator (via OpenShift Console or CLI):

oc apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stackrox/stackrox/master/install/stackrox-operator.yaml


Ensure the operator is running and stackrox namespace pods are healthy.

2. Create ArgoCD ServiceAccount, Role, and RoleBinding

Apply the RBAC manifests for ArgoCD:

oc apply -f argocd-rbac.yaml


This will create:

ServiceAccount: argocd-stackrox-sa in openshift-gitops

Role: argocd-stackrox-role in stackrox

RoleBinding: argocd-stackrox-rb in stackrox

This allows ArgoCD to manage SecurityPolicy resources in the stackrox namespace.

3. Configure ArgoCD Application

Apply the ArgoCD application manifest:

oc apply -f argocd-app.yaml


This will:

Sync the rhacs_policies/deploy/ directory to the stackrox namespace

Automate deployment of SecurityPolicies

Self-heal and prune changes as needed

4. Add / Update SecurityPolicies

Place your YAML files under rhacs_policies/deploy/.
Example:

rhacs_policies/deploy/require-readonly-rootfs.yaml


Commit and push changes:

git add rhacs_policies/deploy/require-readonly-rootfs.yaml
git commit -m "Add Require Read-Only Root Filesystem policy"
git push origin main


ArgoCD will automatically detect the change and apply the SecurityPolicy.

5. Verify SecurityPolicy Deployment

Check the SecurityPolicy status:

oc get securitypolicy require-readonly-rootfs -n stackrox -o yaml


Expected output:

status.accepted: true

policyId populated

No validation errors

You can also view policies in the RHACS UI.

6. Example SecurityPolicy
apiVersion: config.stackrox.io/v1alpha1
kind: SecurityPolicy
metadata:
  name: require-readonly-rootfs
  namespace: stackrox
spec:
  policyName: Require Read-Only Root Filesystem
  categories:
    - Kubernetes Security
  severity: MEDIUM_SEVERITY
  lifecycleStages:
    - DEPLOY
  policySections:
    - name: Security Context
      description: Containers must run with a read-only root filesystem
      policyGroups:
        - name: Read-Only Root Filesystem Group
          fieldName: Read-Only Root Filesystem
          values:
            - value: "true"
          policies:
            - name: Require Read-Only Root Filesystem
              description: Containers must run with a read-only root filesystem
              type: K8S

Notes

Always verify fieldName and values in SecurityPolicy YAMLs against RHACS documentation.

Use the status field of SecurityPolicy to debug validation errors.

All new SecurityPolicies should follow the same policySections structure for ArgoCD automation.
